; Current sound effect: the 8-byte record being played
;
; #R$871A copies the record of the requested effect from #R$87F2 here when the effect starts and updates the first
; four fields while it plays. The record format is the one of the table:
; .
; +0 byte: PERIOD, the loop count between two flips of the speaker in the burst of a frame (0 means one click only). The
; smaller it is, the higher the pitch.
; .
; +1 byte: STEP, added to PERIOD after every frame with 8-bit wrap-around ($FA is -6); a negative step raises the pitch
; .
; +2 byte: FRAMES, the frames (bursts) left in the current segment; the table value is the length of the first segment
; .
; +3 byte: SEGMENTS, the number of segments of the effect, counted down as they end (the noise effect uses it as its
; frame counter)
; .
; +4 byte: MODE, what happens to PERIOD at the start of the next segment: 0 PERIOD = BASE, 1 BASE -= 2 and PERIOD = BASE,
; 2 BASE += 2 and PERIOD = BASE, 3 or more PERIOD goes on and STEP changes sign
; .
; +5 byte: BASE, the PERIOD a new segment starts from (changed by modes 1 and 2)
; .
; +6 byte: RELOAD, the length in frames of the second and later segments (0 means 256)
; .
; +7 byte: NEXT, the effect to start when this one has ended, 0 for none
@label=SoundPeriod
g$87EA DEFB $00
@label=SoundStep
 $87EB DEFB $00
@label=SoundFrames
 $87EC DEFB $00
@label=SoundSegments
 $87ED DEFB $00
@label=SoundMode
 $87EE DEFB $00
@label=SoundBase
 $87EF DEFB $00
@label=SoundReload
 $87F0 DEFB $00
@label=SoundNext
 $87F1 DEFB $00
